# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CODEOWNERS — the human gate for the Agentic SDLC demo
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file, combined with the `main` branch ruleset, is what makes the demo
# real. The ruleset is configured as:
#
#     required_approving_review_count : 0
#     require_code_owner_review       : true
#     required status check           : ci
#
# Consequences:
#
#   • A pull request touching ONLY paths with no owner below needs ZERO
#     approvals. CI passes, auto-merge fires, and it deploys itself. No human
#     is involved at any point.
#
#   • A pull request touching ANY owned path below requires that owner's
#     approval. GitHub blocks the merge button. No workflow, no token and no
#     agent can bypass it — including the agent that opened the pull request.
#
# The omissions are as deliberate as the entries. `src/features/ui/`,
# `src/features/checkout/`, `src/styles/`, `demo/` and `tests/` have NO owner,
# because presentation code and pure, well-tested functions do not need a human
# to look at a one-line fix at 3am.
#
# Risk decides who has to say yes — not priority.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Identity and sessions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A wrong change here either locks every customer out, or lets revoked and
# expired sessions keep working. Always gated.
/src/features/auth/          @pakbaz

# ── Shared transport ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by every feature. Timeout and retry changes propagate everywhere at
# once, so a human confirms the blast radius.
/src/features/api/           @pakbaz

# ── Infrastructure as code ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data exposure and availability. Cannot be rolled back by reverting a render.
/infra/                      @pakbaz

# ── The automation itself ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything able to edit the pipeline can disable its own guardrails. This is
# the most important line in the file: it stops an agent from widening its own
# permissions, editing the policy gate, or removing this very file.
/.github/                    @pakbaz

# ── The demo control plane ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# setup/seed/reset/doctor drive the repository settings and the branch
# ruleset. Anything able to rewrite these can turn the gate off.
/scripts/                    @pakbaz
/Makefile                    @pakbaz

# ── Dependency and build surface ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supply chain. A new transitive dependency deserves a human.
/package.json                @pakbaz
/package-lock.json           @pakbaz
/vite.config.ts              @pakbaz
/playwright.config.ts        @pakbaz
/eslint.config.js            @pakbaz
/tsconfig.json               @pakbaz
/tsconfig.app.json           @pakbaz
/tsconfig.node.json          @pakbaz
/.gitattributes              @pakbaz


# ── Intentionally UNOWNED (the automated lane) ──────────────────────────────
#   /src/features/ui/            presentation only
#   /src/features/checkout/      pure, fully unit-tested money maths
#   /src/features/dashboard/     read-only visualisation
#   /src/styles/                 CSS
#   /tests/                      test coverage
#   /demo/                       documentation
#   /README.md                   documentation
